    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687-a4">

                <pb facs="1197" n="1103" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg1103"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Viscount Palmerston
                        to Sir Stratford Canning.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1850-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 24,
                        1850</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch of the 26th
                    November, inclosing a translation of the firman in favor of Protestants in the
                    Turkish Empire which has received the sanction of the Sultan, and I have to
                    state to your excellency that the version of that document inclosed in your
                    dispatch appears to Her Majesty’s Government to be as complete and as
                    satisfactory as possible; and Her Majesty’s Government look forward with extreme
                    interest to the permanently beneficial effects which this firman must
                    necessarily produce.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Palmerstoh.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
